{"version": 2, "width": 104, "height": 46, "theme": null}
[0.3, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "\u001b[1;36m== 1. Human stores the secret ONCE (hidden prompt; never typed into chat)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m$ sealref set demo API_KEY      # prompt hidden; demo pipes the fake value\u001b[0m\r\nsealref://demo/API_KEY\r\n\r\n"]
[3.3, "o", "\u001b[1;36m== 2. The agent only ever sees the ref\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m$ sealref keys demo\u001b[0m\r\nAPI_KEY  sealref://demo/API_KEY\r\n\r\n"]
[4.8, "o", "\u001b[1;36m== 3+4. 'sealref run' injects it into the command's env; output is scrubbed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m$ sealref run --ref sealref://demo/API_KEY -- sh -c 'echo \"Authorization: Bearer $API_KEY\"; env | grep API_KEY'\u001b[0m\r\nAuthorization: Bearer \u00abredacted:demo/API_KEY\u00bb\r\nAPI_KEY=\u00abredacted:demo/API_KEY\u00bb\r\n\u001b[33m$ # the command really had the value (length only):\u001b[0m\r\nlen=33\r\n\u001b[33m$ # the base64 form is scrubbed too (URL-encoded as well):\u001b[0m\r\n\u00abredacted:demo/API_KEY\u00bb\r\n\r\n"]
[6.3, "o", "\u001b[1;36m== 5. What lands in the transcript\u001b[0m\r\n  PASTE IN CHAT                              (all of this is in the transcript)\r\n    user : here is my key: sk-demo-FAKE-9f3a1c7e5b2d4806a1f0\r\n    agent: curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer sk-demo-FAKE-9f3a1c7e5b2d4806a1f0\" ...\r\n    tool : {\"auth\":\"sk-demo-FAKE-9f3a1c7e5b2d4806a1f0\"}\r\n    + shell history, logs, context window re-sent every turn, provider logs\r\n\r\n  SEALREF                                    (the value appears nowhere)\r\n    user : (typed into a hidden prompt, not chat)\r\n    agent: sealref run --ref sealref://demo/API_KEY -- curl ...\r\n    tool : {\"auth\":\"\u00abredacted:demo/API_KEY\u00bb\"}\r\n    value lives only in the OS keystore\r\n\r\n"]
[7.8, "o", "\u001b[1;36m== 6. Agent usage (MCP, Claude Code)\u001b[0m\r\n  claude mcp add sealref --scope user -- uv run --directory /path/to/sealref \\\r\n      --with \"mcp==1.29.0\" python -m sealref.mcp_server\r\n  agent calls: has_secret(\"stripe\",\"API_KEY\") -> true\r\n               request_secret(\"stripe\",\"API_KEY\",\"charge test\") -> \"sealref://stripe/API_KEY\"\r\n  agent runs : sealref run --ref sealref://stripe/API_KEY -- ./charge.sh\r\n\r\n"]
[9.3, "o", "\u001b[1;36m== 7. Honest limit: scrubbing is exact-match, not magic\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m$ sealref run ... -- sh -c 'echo $API_KEY | rev'\u001b[0m\r\n0f1a6084d2b5e7c1a3f9-EKAF-omed-ks\r\n  ^ a transformed value gets through. sealref stops accidents, not a hostile agent.\r\n\r\n"]
[10.8, "o", "\u001b[1;36m== Cleanup\u001b[0m\r\nremaining demo keys: 0\r\n"]
[14.3, "o", ""]
